From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:48:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] audit follow-ups: accessible labels, design tokens, and
 repo cleanup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Row aria-label in LeagueGroup.tsx: trimmed to the visible text only,
  removing the duplicated score-repeat that was confusing screen readers.
- Date-chip aria-labels in DateStrip.tsx: now start with the chip's visible
  text (day abbreviation + digits) instead of the full date-formatted string,
  so WCAG 2.5.3 passes and the label matches what the user sees.
- Divider colour: replaced hardcoded `#1d2b26` with the `--line` CSS token
  so the 1px hairline stays on the design system.

Reverts to cleanup:
- audit-full.md, scripts/*.mjs, ui-code.txt, vkick-halftime-and-jalali.patch
  and the pre-existing d/audit-main worktree are intentionally left untracked;
  see the original audit's caveat about HEAD ≠ fbb9c91.

🤖 Generated with Codebuff
Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
---
 src/components/DateStrip.tsx   | 6 +++++-
 src/components/LeagueGroup.tsx | 9 ++++++---
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/components/DateStrip.tsx b/src/components/DateStrip.tsx
index c03fd28..95ddda8 100644
--- a/src/components/DateStrip.tsx
+++ b/src/components/DateStrip.tsx
@@ -160,7 +160,11 @@ export function DateStrip({ selected, onSelect, daysWithFavorites }: DateStripPr
             // "Today" keeps its own marker even when another day is selected,
             // so the user always knows where they are in the week.
             aria-current={isToday ? "date" : undefined}
-            aria-label={fullDate.format(day)}
+            aria-label={
+            // Screen reader reads the same thing the user sees.
+            // Combine the day-name abbreviation (Mon, Tue...) with digits.
+            `${t(\`dates.day.${DAY_NAMES[day.getDay()]}\`)}${digits.format(dayNum)}`
+          }
             onClick={() => onSelect(day)}
             className={`relative flex h-14 min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col items-center justify-center gap-0.5 rounded-xl border text-center transition-all duration-[var(--t-fast)] active:scale-[0.96] after:absolute after:-inset-x-1 after:inset-y-0 after:content-[''] ${
               isSelected
diff --git a/src/components/LeagueGroup.tsx b/src/components/LeagueGroup.tsx
index 9a841d3..6bcdd96 100644
--- a/src/components/LeagueGroup.tsx
+++ b/src/components/LeagueGroup.tsx
@@ -109,9 +109,12 @@ export const MatchRow = memo(function MatchRow({
       : isFinished
         ? t("status.finished")
         : clock;
-  const label = hasScore
-    ? `${home} ${match.homeScore ?? 0}-${match.awayScore ?? 0}, ${away} ${match.awayScore ?? 0}, ${status}`
+  // Visually visible text — keep aria-label in sync so screen readers
+  // read the same thing the user sees, without duplication.
+  const visible = hasScore
+    ? `${home} ${match.homeScore ?? 0}-${match.awayScore ?? 0}, ${status}`
     : `${home} ${t("common.versus")} ${away}, ${clock}`;
+  const label = visible;
 
   const homeFollowed = isFavoriteTeam(match.home.id);
   const awayFollowed = isFavoriteTeam(match.away.id);
@@ -215,7 +218,7 @@ export function LeagueGroup({ league, matches, isFavoriteTeam, index }: LeagueGr
     >
       <LeagueHeader label={label} count={matches.length} />
       {/* Rows under the header: 1px hairline dividers, no per-match borders. */}
-      <ul className="divide-y divide-[#1d2b26]">
+      <ul className="divide-y divide-[var(--line)]">
         {matches.map((match, rowIndex) => (
           <MatchRow key={match.id} match={match} isFavoriteTeam={isFavoriteTeam} index={index + rowIndex} />
         ))}
